    "summary": "Tight late‑1972 set with stellar China>Rider and soaring Sugar Magnolia",
    "blurb": "The Detroit show captures a high‑energy, rock‑n‑roll oriented set. Highlights include a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider, crisp Box of Rain, and a rousing Sugar Magnolia > Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad medley. Audience tape quality is good with only slight hiss.",
    "review": "October 30, 1972 at Ford Auditorium finds the Dead in fine form as they cruise through a tight late‑1972 set. Jerry’s lead lines on China Cat Sunflower glide into the classic Rider segue with crystal clarity, while Phil underpins the groove with his trademark melodic bass. Bob provides solid rhythmic support and Keith adds tasteful keyboard colors that lift the band without overwhelming the mix. The second set builds momentum through a bright Sugar Magnolia that flows seamlessly into Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad, culminating in an earnest Uncle John’s Band encore. Though it’s an audience recording, the tape retains enough ambience and detail to let listeners feel the room’s excitement.",
